  "id": "dorsolateral-column",
  "term": "dorsolateral column",
  "definition": "The dorsolateral column usually refers here to the dorsolateral periaqueductal gray, a midbrain area involved in processing threatening and other strongly aversive experiences. In learning research, it is described as helping link life-threatening events to fear learning through its connections with hypothalamic and thalamic pathways.",
